WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.164 --> 00:00:01.764
Hello there.

2
00:00:00.582 --> 00:00:06.154
My name is Walter Engstrom, and I'm a patient at
Kestrel Falls Community Hospital.

3
00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:10.852
Laura Hemmingsen told me the hospital is
changing the computer system that holds

4
00:00:10.852 --> 00:00:12.895
patient records, and she wanted to
hear from patients, too.

5
00:00:12.895 --> 00:00:14.009
So here I am.

6
00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:17.984
I'm seventy-eight, and I've been coming to
Kestrel Falls for most of my life.

7
00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:22.444
I farmed just outside town for forty-five
years, so I know half the county.

8
00:00:22.444 --> 00:00:25.075
I see the heart doctor at the
clinic every few months,

9
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:27.112
and I take six or seven pills a day.

10
00:00:27.112 --> 00:00:29.728
My daughter Beth keeps track of
them better than I do.

11
00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:35.239
When I hear the hospital is changing its
records system, what worries me?

12
00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:37.812
I hear on the news about
hospitals getting hacked,

13
00:00:37.812 --> 00:00:39.333
and people's records ending up
who knows where.

14
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:44.262
So when they say they're moving all the
records to a new computer system,

15
00:00:44.262 --> 00:00:46.053
my first thought is: will mine
get lost on the way,

16
00:00:46.053 --> 00:00:50.028
or will somebody see what they shouldn't?

17
00:00:50.028 --> 00:00:52.200
I've got fifty years of records here.

18
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.122
My heart, my knee surgery, all of it.

19
00:00:53.122 --> 00:00:57.490
What would help me feel confident is somebody
telling me in plain words what you're

20
00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.293
doing to keep it safe.

21
00:00:59.293 --> 00:01:01.737
Not a long letter full of legal language.

22
00:01:01.737 --> 00:01:05.148
Just: here's what's moving,
here's who can see it,

23
00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:06.903
here's what we're doing about hackers.

24
00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:10.430
And if something does go wrong, tell me.

25
00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.030
Don't hide it.

26
00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.432
I don't use the patient portal much.

27
00:01:12.432 --> 00:01:15.113
The password rules are a
nuisance and I forget it.

28
00:01:15.113 --> 00:01:19.363
Capital letters, numbers, a symbol, and
then it makes you change it.

29
00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:21.731
I tried once on the phone and gave up.

30
00:01:21.731 --> 00:01:24.658
What I'd like is simple access
to my own records.

31
00:01:24.658 --> 00:01:27.514
My medicines, my appointments, my test
results, in plain words.

32
00:01:27.514 --> 00:01:32.506
Not "your lab value is within the reference
range." Just tell me if it's good or

33
00:01:32.506 --> 00:01:33.106
bad and what to do.

34
00:01:32.506 --> 00:01:35.405
For help with my health care,
it's Beth, mostly.

35
00:01:35.405 --> 00:01:40.259
She lives about an hour away, but she calls
every day and comes when I have

36
00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:40.859
appointments.

37
00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:44.063
I'm happy for Beth to help me with
appointments and my pill list.

38
00:01:44.063 --> 00:01:45.953
She's better at it than I am,
and I trust her.

39
00:01:45.953 --> 00:01:47.442
But some things are mine.

40
00:01:47.442 --> 00:01:49.760
I saw a counselor for a while
after my wife died,

41
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:54.505
and I'd rather those notes stay
private, even from Beth.

42
00:01:54.505 --> 00:01:55.691
It's not that I'm ashamed of it.

43
00:01:55.691 --> 00:01:57.356
It's just mine.

44
00:01:57.356 --> 00:01:59.865
I'd want to be asked before
anyone sees those.

45
00:01:59.865 --> 00:02:04.034
I'd hope a new system would let me say who sees
what, instead of all or nothing.

46
00:02:04.034 --> 00:02:08.164
Here's what I'd want the people
planning this to know.

47
00:02:08.164 --> 00:02:10.144
Remember that some of us are old
and don't do computers.

48
00:02:10.144 --> 00:02:14.157
Keep a phone number where a
real person answers.

49
00:02:14.157 --> 00:02:16.948
Don't make the portal the only way
to get things done.

50
00:02:16.948 --> 00:02:20.399
And when you switch over, make sure my
doctor still has my pill list.

51
00:02:20.399 --> 00:02:22.402
I'd hate for something to get dropped.

52
00:02:22.402 --> 00:02:24.659
How should the hospital tell me
about the change?

53
00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:29.754
A letter in the mail, and somebody
mentions it at my appointment.

54
00:02:29.754 --> 00:02:30.831
My doctor, ideally.

55
00:02:30.831 --> 00:02:31.430
I trust her.

56
00:02:30.831 --> 00:02:32.118
Not just an email.

57
00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:34.701
And I read the paper, so put
it in there too.

58
00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:37.736
The Kestrel Falls paper still
comes out every week.

59
00:02:37.736 --> 00:02:42.367
If you offered help setting up the new
portal, would I use it?

60
00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.851
If it was a person, sitting with me, yes.

61
00:02:43.851 --> 00:02:47.210
Maybe at the clinic before an appointment.

62
00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.457
With Beth there.

63
00:02:49.457 --> 00:02:52.775
If I have to do it alone on my
phone, probably not.

64
00:02:52.775 --> 00:02:55.752
And if you make the password simpler,
I might actually use it.

65
00:02:55.752 --> 00:02:57.214
Thank you for asking.

66
00:02:57.214 --> 00:02:58.120
Nobody asked last time.

